# rb.sh's build host per worktree: the first line whose bash glob matches the worktree's directory name wins.
# Hosts (lead 11-27; vibex6 is gone): vibe2 (16 cores, 30 GB: the land queue + psui's builds), vibex7 (main's watcher, core's
# builds, qa's 02:00-04:05 speed window), vibex8 (bool, skasm, qa's suites, nightly T2) (8 cores, 29 GB each, 2 slots). The user's Mac (12 cores) takes half: 2 slots of 3 jobs at nice 19 (user 11-21:
# "half is fine"). Heavy one-off probes: NOSHAPE_RB_HOST=<the idlest host>.
bool2*    vibex8
bool*     vibex8
core*     vibex7
blend*    vibex7
dev*      vibex7
psui*     vibe2
skasm*    vibex8
dx*       vibe2
asm*      vibex8
studios*  vibex7
cliapp*   vibex7
appicon*  vibex7
*         vibe2
